Inputs and all nested message arrays are guaranteed non-null. Dispatch messages synchronously in array order. For each message, invoke `handler.onMessage` exactly once with a defensive copy and a new acknowledgement object dedicated to that invocation. Calling `complete()` one or more times acknowledges that message; repeated calls are idempotent. After the handler returns, record whether it acknowledged the message. Return those results in a newly allocated boolean array.

Handler mutations to the delivered byte array must never change `messages` or affect any other callback. The method must not otherwise mutate the input.

