`normalizeProperties(String input)` parses semicolon-separated `key=value` fields and returns their canonical serialization. An empty input returns an empty string.

Both components use percent escapes of the form `%HH`, where each `H` is a hexadecimal digit. Unescaped characters must be printable ASCII and cannot be `%`, `;`, or `=`. After decoding, keys must contain only ASCII letters, digits, or hyphens and must be converted to lowercase. Values may contain any printable ASCII character.

If the same normalized key occurs more than once, the last value wins. Serialize fields in ascending normalized-key order. Separate fields with semicolons. In output values, encode `%`, `;`, and `=` as `%25`, `%3B`, and `%3D`; all other characters remain literal. Reject invalid input with `IllegalArgumentException`.

