Repair the following complete JavaScript source file and return a corrected complete source file.

The exported `rankChoices(ballots)` function receives valid ballot objects shaped as `{ voter, choice, sequence }`. A voter may appear more than once. Only that voter's ballot with the greatest numeric `sequence` may count; if the voter has multiple ballots at that sequence, the earliest one in the input counts.

Return one `{ choice, count }` object for every choice represented by the selected ballots. Rank choices by descending count, breaking ties by ascending JavaScript code-unit string order of `choice`.

The current implementation counts duplicate voters:

```javascript
function compareText(a, b) {
  if (a < b) return -1;
  if (a > b) return 1;
  return 0;
}

function rankChoices(ballots) {
  const counts = new Map();

  for (const ballot of ballots) {
    counts.set(ballot.choice, (counts.get(ballot.choice) || 0) + 1);
  }

  return Array.from(counts, ([choice, count]) => ({ choice, count }))
    .sort((a, b) => {
      if (a.count !== b.count) return b.count - a.count;
      return compareText(a.choice, b.choice);
    });
}

module.exports = { rankChoices };
```

