```

`width` must be a positive integer; otherwise the factory throws `RangeError`. `push` must reject non-finite values with `RangeError`. It appends the value, removes the oldest value when the retained sample count would exceed `width`, and returns the arithmetic mean of the retained window. `mean` returns that same mean, or `undefined` before any value has been pushed. `count` returns the number of retained samples.

Maintain the rolling sum incrementally rather than recomputing it by traversing the full window for every mean. Each factory call must create an isolated window: pushing values or evicting samples in one instance must not affect any other instance.

