The public API is `normalize_rename_spec(spec)`. `spec` must be a dictionary whose only key is `jobs`. Its value must be a list. Every list element must be a dictionary with exactly the string-valued keys `source` and `target`. The same job dictionary may occur at multiple positions in the list.

Normalize both paths in every job by stripping surrounding whitespace, changing `\\` separators to `/`, removing empty components and `.` components, and joining the remaining components with `/`. Reject an empty normalized path or any path containing a `..` component by raising `ValueError`.

The returned object must be a recursive deep copy: no mutable object in it may alias a mutable object from `spec`. Internal alias relationships must nevertheless be preserved. In particular, if two input positions reference the same job dictionary, the corresponding output positions must reference the same copied dictionary. The input must remain unchanged. Raise `ValueError` when the structure does not match the specified format.

