Implement `solution.rs` as a standard-library-only Rust library providing a keyed event dispatcher.

Expose exactly this public API:

```rust
use std::collections::BTreeMap;

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Event {
    pub kind: u8,
    pub value: i32,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum HandlerFlow {
    Continue,
    Stop,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct DispatchReport {
    pub invoked: usize,
    pub stopped: bool,
}

pub type Handler = Box<dyn FnMut(&Event) -> HandlerFlow>;

pub struct Dispatcher {
    // private fields
}

impl Dispatcher {
    pub fn new() -> Self;
    pub fn on(&mut self, kind: u8, handler: Handler);
    pub fn dispatch(&mut self, event: &Event) -> DispatchReport;
}
```

Handlers registered for a kind execute in registration order. `dispatch` must invoke only handlers whose key equals `event.kind`. A `Continue` result advances to the next handler, while `Stop` ends only that dispatch and sets `stopped` to true. `invoked` counts callbacks actually called. If no handler matches, both report fields are zero-equivalent.

Completion state must be isolated between dispatch calls: a handler stopping one event must not prevent any later event, including one of the same kind, from starting with its first handler. Separate `Dispatcher` instances must also share no state.

Do not use a filesystem, network, clock, randomness, external package, framework, or `main` function.

Return only the complete source file; do not include Markdown fences or prose.

use std::collections::BTreeMap;

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Event {
    pub kind: u8,
    pub value: i32,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum HandlerFlow {
    Continue,
    Stop,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct DispatchReport {
    pub invoked: usize,
    pub stopped: bool,
}

pub type Handler = Box<dyn FnMut(&Event) -> HandlerFlow>;

pub struct Dispatcher {
    handlers: BTreeMap<u8, Vec<Handler>>,
}

impl Dispatcher {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            handlers: BTreeMap::new(),
        }
    }

    pub fn on(&mut self, kind: u8, handler: Handler) {
        self.handlers.entry(kind).or_default().push(handler);
    }

    pub fn dispatch(&mut self, event: &Event) -> DispatchReport {
        let mut invoked = 0;
        let mut stopped = false;

        if let Some(handlers) = self.handlers.get_mut(&event.kind) {
            for handler in handlers {
                invoked += 1;
                if handler(event) == HandlerFlow::Stop {
                    stopped = true;
                    break;
                }
            }
        }

        DispatchReport { invoked, stopped }
    }
}

