Implement `solution.rs` as a standard-library-only Rust library for routing byte signals to stream-specific listeners.

Expose exactly this public API:

```rust
use std::collections::BTreeMap;

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum ListenerState {
    Listening,
    Complete,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct EmitReport {
    pub invoked: usize,
    pub completed: usize,
}

pub type Listener = Box<dyn FnMut(&[u8]) -> ListenerState>;

pub struct SignalHub {
    // private fields
}

impl SignalHub {
    pub fn new() -> Self;
    pub fn subscribe(&mut self, stream_id: u32, listener: Listener);
    pub fn emit(&mut self, stream_id: u32, payload: &[u8]) -> EmitReport;
}
```

A listener belongs exclusively to the `stream_id` supplied to `subscribe`. `emit` invokes only listeners for the specified stream, in subscription order. Each callback receives the same payload slice supplied to `emit`.

Returning `Listening` keeps that listener subscribed. Returning `Complete` means the callback has completed: count it in both `invoked` and `completed`, then remove it before the next emission. Removing a completed listener must not skip the following listener during the current emission. A stream without listeners returns zero for both counts.

Listener collections and completion effects must remain isolated by stream: emitting or completing listeners on one stream must neither invoke, remove, nor reorder listeners on another stream. Separate hubs must share no state.

Do not use a filesystem, network, clock, randomness, external package, framework, or `main` function.

Return only the complete source file; do not include Markdown fences or prose.

use std::collections::BTreeMap;

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum ListenerState {
    Listening,
    Complete,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct EmitReport {
    pub invoked: usize,
    pub completed: usize,
}

pub type Listener = Box<dyn FnMut(&[u8]) -> ListenerState>;

pub struct SignalHub {
    listeners: BTreeMap<u32, Vec<Listener>>,
}

impl SignalHub {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            listeners: BTreeMap::new(),
        }
    }

    pub fn subscribe(&mut self, stream_id: u32, listener: Listener) {
        self.listeners.entry(stream_id).or_default().push(listener);
    }

    pub fn emit(&mut self, stream_id: u32, payload: &[u8]) -> EmitReport {
        let mut invoked = 0;
        let mut completed = 0;

        let empty = {
            let Some(listeners) = self.listeners.get_mut(&stream_id) else {
                return EmitReport { invoked, completed };
            };

            let mut index = 0;
            while index < listeners.len() {
                invoked += 1;
                if listeners[index](payload) == ListenerState::Complete {
                    completed += 1;
                    let _ = listeners.remove(index);
                } else {
                    index += 1;
                }
            }
            listeners.is_empty()
        };

        if empty {
            self.listeners.remove(&stream_id);
        }

        EmitReport { invoked, completed }
    }
}

